From 9b51cf6e36b5bf7704c509ff7fa6fef1fc6363d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:46:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] A refused Save as a new map keeps the map maker open with
 the GM's edits, and Save map then saves the edit

Two causes, both of the map maker's asNew flag. Save as a new map passed whatever save answered to shell.done, and a
refused save answers undefined, which done took as the window's answer and closed it. And the flag that told save to
write a new id stayed set after the refusal, so the next Save map added a new map in place of the edit. The id a save
writes is now save's argument (saveAs), the flag is gone, and Save as a new map closes the window only on a saved map,
as the shell's own Save does. Audit BUG-views-4; held by the two Save as a new map cases of tests/e2e/maps.e2e.ts.
